        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chromium partially supports `{align,justify,place}-self` with absolute positioning]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29342</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29342"/>
        <updated>2026-05-22T14:46:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds partial implementation flags and notes for <code class="notranslate">align-self</code>, <code class="notranslate">justify-self</code>, and <code class="notranslate">place-self</code> for all browsers, when they apply to absolutely positioned elements.</p>
<p dir="auto">I tested this in Safari, Firefox, and Chrome, and discussed with Mozilla engineers <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/dshin-moz/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/dshin-moz">@dshin-moz</a> and <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/emilio/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/emilio">@emilio</a>.<br>
My understanding is that there's a missing piece in all browsers where you can't just apply the above properties and expect them to work on their own. They also require a non-auto <code class="notranslate">inset</code> value.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Test case: <a href="https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965" rel="nofollow">https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965</a></p>
<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..wW5Lf5pDIzxylNj_KPZ6jmmMtbJc5tGDxYNosmo4UDE"><img width="859" height="685" alt="image" src="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..wW5Lf5pDIzxylNj_KPZ6jmmMtbJc5tGDxYNosmo4UDE" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 685px;; aspect-ratio: 859 / 685; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px" class="js-gh-image-fallback"></a>
<p dir="auto">The red box should be centered in the gray box.</p>
<p dir="auto">Code:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;style&gt;
  .parent { position: absolute; inset: 20vmin; background: gray; }
  .child { position: absolute; width: 50%; aspect-ratio: 1; background: red; justify-self: center; }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;parent&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;child&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-c1">&lt;!DOCTYPE html<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span></span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">style</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
  .<span class="pl-c1">parent</span> { <span class="pl-c1">position</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> absolute; <span class="pl-c1">inset</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> <span class="pl-c1">20<span class="pl-smi">vmin</span></span>; <span class="pl-c1">background</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> gray; }
  .<span class="pl-c1">child</span> { <span class="pl-c1">position</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> absolute; <span class="pl-c1">width</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> <span class="pl-c1">50<span class="pl-smi">%</span></span>; <span class="pl-c1">aspect-ratio</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> <span class="pl-c1">1</span>; <span class="pl-c1">background</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> red; <span class="pl-c1">justify-self</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> center; }
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class="pl-ent">style</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">div</span> <span class="pl-c1">class</span>="<span class="pl-s">parent</span>"<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
  <span class="pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class="pl-ent">div</span> <span class="pl-c1">class</span>="<span class="pl-s">child</span>"<span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span><span class="pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class="pl-ent">div</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class="pl-ent">div</span><span class="pl-kos">&gt;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Adding <code class="notranslate">inset:0;</code> on the child element makes it work.</p>
<p dir="auto">I'm not entirely sure I'm reading the spec correctly though, and the placement of auto-inset abspos elements may actually be correct. But, WPT seems to show browser differences in this area at least: <a href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned" rel="nofollow">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Firefox bug that was filed as a result of my discussion with Mozilla engineers: <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174</a></li>
<li>Related Chromium issue: <a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648" rel="nofollow">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
